 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Dominated by sorting, $O(N \log N)$, where $N$ is the number of points. The subsequent unique and cumulative sum operations are linear $O(N)$ or proportional to the number of unique voxels $K$.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for storing intermediate arrays (grid, keys, sorted colors). The output size is $O(K)$, where $K$ is the number of active voxels.
-- **Performance:** Efficient for moderate-sized point clouds on CPU due to vectorized NumPy operations. Performance degrades if $N$ is extremely large due to memory allocation for sorting.
-- **Strengths:** Deterministic output, simple implementation, no GPU required, handles attribute averaging naturally.
-- **Limitations:** Sorting bottleneck for very large $N$; memory intensive for high-resolution grids with sparse points if not filtered; not suitable for real-time streaming without batching.
