 ## Background
-Vectorized Voxelization is a practical implementation detail often found in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) pipelines and other point cloud processing frameworks. It is not a distinct academic algorithm with a single seminal paper but rather a standard engineering pattern for efficient CPU-side voxelization. The specific implementation cited here is from the `3dgs-voxelizer-Omni` repository, which adapts these techniques for processing 3DGS data.
